  "answer": "To reduce the risk of robots causing accidents (such as crashing or endangering people and hardware) while learning tasks that alter their step response to control commands, the SafeOpt-MC algorithm has been proposed (https://arxiv.org/abs/1602.04450). This approach mitigates risk by decoupling performance optimization from safety constraints and restricting real-system evaluations to a high-confidence safe set (https://arxiv.org/abs/1602.04450). The mechanism utilizes a Gaussian-process (GP) surrogate model over both performance and multiple constraints; it iteratively updates the GP models and expands the known-safe region by certifying neighboring parameters via Lipschitz continuity or direct GP lower bounds (https://arxiv.org/abs/1602.04450). By selecting the next parameters based on uncertainty, the algorithm safely balances exploration and exploitation without violating physical or operational limits (https://arxiv.org/abs/1602.04450)."
